{"name":"Midsummer Field","hex":"#88cc44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midsummer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The period around the summer solstice; around June 21st in the northern hemisphere.","The first day of summer."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or occurring in the middle of summer."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midsummer"},{"term":"field","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A land area free of woodland, cities, and towns; an area of open country.","The open country near or belonging to a town or city."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To intercept or catch (a ball) and play it.","To be the team catching and throwing the ball, as opposed to hitting it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midsummer","blocks":[{"text":"Midsummer or Midsommar is a celebration of the season of summer, taking place on or near the date of the summer solstice in the Northern Hemisphere, the longest day of the year. The name midsummer mainly refers to summer solstice festivals of European origin. These cultures traditionally regard it as the middle of summer, with the season beginning on May Day. Although the summer solstice falls on 20, 21 or 22 June in the Northern Hemisphere, it was traditionally reckoned to fall on 23–24 June in much of Europe. These dates were Christianized as Saint John's Eve and Saint John's Day. It is usually celebrated with outdoor gatherings that include bonfires, maypole dancing and feasting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Mittsommerfest_in_Norwegen%2C_Insel_Tysnes_IMG_4425WI.jpg/330px-Mittsommerfest_in_Norwegen%2C_Insel_Tysnes_IMG_4425WI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midsummer","wikidata":"Q154502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg/500px-Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg/500px-Midsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Midsummer Eve Bonfire by Norwegian artist Nikolai Astrup (c.1915)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidsummer-eve-bonfire-nikolai-astrup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG/500px-KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG/500px-KastelholmMidsommarst.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A maypole at Midsummer near the Kastelholm Castle in Sund, Åland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKastelholmMidsommarst.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/DIMG_5456_%284735649602%29.jpg/500px-DIMG_5456_%284735649602%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/DIMG_5456_%284735649602%29.jpg/1280px-DIMG_5456_%284735649602%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/DIMG_5456_%284735649602%29.jpg/500px-DIMG_5456_%284735649602%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swedes celebrating Midsummer, Möja island in the Stockholm archipelago","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADIMG_5456_(4735649602).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Nestinar.bulgari.jpg/500px-Nestinar.bulgari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb